  "body": "## What changed\n\nSix library machines from the makers' public pages, on the **Grbl 1.1** post:\n\n| Machine | Travel X x Y x Z, mm | Spindle |\n|---|---|---|\n| Carbide 3D Shapeoko 5 Pro 4x4 | 1237 x 1237 x 155 | not stated (the owner chooses the router) |\n| Carbide 3D Shapeoko 5 Pro 4x2 | 1237 x 623 x 155 | not stated |\n| Carbide 3D Shapeoko 5 Pro 2x2 | 623 x 623 x 155 | not stated |\n| Inventables X-Carve 2021 1000 mm | 749.3 x 749.3 x 114.3 | 10,000-30,000 rpm, 0.8 kW (Makita) |\n| Inventables X-Carve Pro 4x4 | 1219.2 x 1219.2 x 101.6 | 8,000-24,000 rpm, 1.5 kW (VFD) |\n| Inventables X-Carve Pro 4x2 | 1219.2 x 609.6 x 101.6 | 8,000-24,000 rpm, 1.5 kW (VFD) |\n\n- Each value has its source in `docs/decisions/3071-hobby-routers.md`: Carbide 3D's \"Shapeoko 5.1 Pro Specifications\" page, and Inventables' machine pages on easel.com.\n- No maker states axis rates or where machine Z0 sits after homing. So the files state no rates and no `safe_retract`. The Grbl post lifts Z in the work offset and stops with `M0` for each tool change (Grbl 1.1 has no `M6`).\n- The X-Carve 2021 model name has no parentheses, because the Grbl post drops them from the first comment line.\n- Registry: `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs` (`MACHINES` and the embedded copies). The user guide (`site/content/guide/check-and-post/machines.md`) names the new frames.\n- Not done: Onefinity. Its current controller is \"Redline CNC Controller powered by Realtime CNC motion software\". No built-in post is confirmed for that dialect, and the series page fills its table by a script. #3071 stays open for it.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/machine/hobby_routers.rs` (in the `machine` directory suite, no new binary):\n- `every_hobby_router_states_only_its_published_figures`\n- `every_tool_change_is_a_stop_after_a_lift_in_the_work_offset`\n- `a_spindle_speed_past_the_stated_maximum_is_refused` (26,000 rpm is refused on the Pro and posts on the 2021 X-Carve)\n- `the_shapeoko_4x4_two_tool_program_is_locked` (golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/grbl/shapeoko_5_pro_4x4_two_tool.nc`)\n- The existing `every_shipped_machine_mounts_and_speaks_its_declaration` lists the six machines.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 766 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (110.6 min). The registry is in the app lib, so the gate selected every app suite.\n- After the move into the `machine` suite: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test machine` 61/61.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-app -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on a real Shapeoko or X-Carve.\n- No heavy lane: the change adds data files and tests.\n\nChangelog: Machines: Carbide 3D Shapeoko 5 Pro (4x4, 4x2, 2x2), Inventables X-Carve 2021 1000 mm and X-Carve Pro (4x4, 4x2) in the machine library, on the Grbl 1.1 post.\n\nRefs #3071\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
